  "street_name": "Rushett Lane",
  "decision_date": "10/09/2025",
  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed residential development, including bungalows, associated curtilages, car parking, and domestic paraphernalia, constitutes inappropriate development in the Metropolitan Green Belt. The development would undermine the purposes of GB1 by reducing the openness of the countryside, causing substantial harm to its sense of openness, and facilitating incremental urbanisation.\r\rThe site is not within an urbanised context but is part of a wider rural landscape, comprising open fields, woodland, and equestrian structures, which continue to serve Green Belt purposes, particularly safeguarding the countryside from encroachment and preventing town mergers. The introduction of four permanent dwellings, with associated activity, would materially increase the built footprint and activity on the site, eroding both the spatial and visual openness, even if it were classed as previously developed land.\r\rThe proposal is therefore contrary to Paragraphs 143, 153-155 of the NPPF (2024), Policy DM5 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), and Policy G2 of the London Plan (2021). \r"
  ],
